# Site Migrator (Cursor)

Codex uses `AGENTS.md`. Claude Code uses `CLAUDE.md` + `.claude/rules/`. See `docs/AI-TOOLS.md`.

Read `AGENTS.md` and `SECURITY.md` before non-trivial changes.

## Scope

- Plugin path: `wp-content/plugins/site-migrator/`
- Pull migration only; source REST + target admin AJAX.

## Security

- Never set `sslverify` to false by default; use `SMIG_Security::sslverify()`.
- Never pass `source_auth` to `wp_localize_script` or front-end JSON.
- Validate SQL identifiers with `SMIG_Security::is_valid_identifier()`.
- Validate remote URLs with `SMIG_Security::validate_source_url()`.
- Admin: `manage_options` + nonce `smig_nonce` on every AJAX handler.

## Code style

- GPL-3.0-or-later; copyright Octarine Studio on new PHP files.
- i18n: `site-migrator` text domain.
- Chunked AJAX; update `smig_resume` option when session state changes.
- Use WordPress APIs (`Plugin_Upgrader`, `plugins_api`, transients, `wp_remote_get`).

## Do not

- Commit `migrator-staging/`, dumps, or auth codes.
- Add customer-specific URLs to placeholders (use `https://example.com`).
- Implement fixes without reproduction or log proof (see workspace No-Speculation rule).

